   {
    "id": "18345326767257632",
    "text": "10 minutes about science and Drakes Equation on Norwegian Prime news - a world record?\n \nWhen it comes to sharing the wonders of space and science with the general public, I think this Norwegian TV2 segment is probably the one I am most proud of in my entire career.\nIt became a very special piece, and a lot of the credit goes to the wonderful and highly skilled presenter Yvonne Fondenes. She had a remarkable ability to make a complicated subject accessible, engaging and natural — and to give us the time and space to really explore it.\n\nWe actually managed to discuss the Drake Equation on prime-time television news! I’m not sure many others have managed to do that — perhaps not even in the United States.\n\nOver the years, I have shown this segment to several of my colleagues at NASA, and they have been genui nely impressed that a Norwegian television news programme was willing to devote so much airtime to such a complex scientific topic.\n\nFor me, communicating science has never just been about explaining facts. It has been about sharing curiosity, excitement and the sense of wonder that comes from trying to understand our universe — and perhaps inspiring others to ask the big questions as well.\n\nLooking back, this TV2 segment represents exactly that, and it remains one of the moments from my career that I treasure the most.\n\nVideo with English subtitles:\nDrakes-TV2-English-subtitled.mp4\n \nNorwegian version::\nNår det gjelder formidling av kunnskap om verdensrommet så tror jeg dette innslaget i TV2 er det jeg er mest stolt av gjennom tidene. Dette ble et veldig bra innslag også takket være den dyktige  programleder Yvonne Fondenes\nsom var veldig flink til å få dette til å fungere. Jeg tror ikke det er noen andre som har klart å diskutere Drake ligning på Prime Time TV nyheter. Selv ikke i USA. Har vist dette til kolleger i NASA og de er ganske imponert at man får til en så lang sending om et så komplisert tema i en nyhetssending.\n \n– Utenkelig at det ikke finnes liv der ute",
