  "caption": "Presented by National Geographic Society in partnership with @Rolex.\n\nPygmy blue whales compete with fin whales for the title of the second-largest animal in the world. They typically roam the world’s oceans, but one group off the coast of New Zealand seems to have settled in the South Taranaki Bight. To better understand the behavior of these marine giants, researchers are studying some of the ocean’s smallest creatures—swarms of krill thriving in the whales’ new home. They hope that by understanding the relationship between the two, they can better understand the effects that warming waters will have on them.\n\nLearn more about this mysterious group of whales at the link in bio.\n\nRolex and the National Geographic Society are partnering on select science-based expeditions to explore, study, and document change in the planet’s unique regions. #PerpetualPlanet.\n\nVideos by National Geographic Society/Impact Story Lab; Photographs by @ralphpace",
